```c
bool ip_csum = (features & (NETIF_F_IP_CSUM | NETIF_F_IPV6_CSUM)) ==
    (NETIF_F_IP_CSUM | NETIF_F_IPV6_CSUM);
bool hw_csum = features & NETIF_F_HW_CSUM;

if (!ip_csum && !hw_csum) {
    netdev_dbg(dev, "Dropping TLS TX HW offload feature since no CSUM feature.\n");
    features &= ~NETIF_F_HW_TLS_TX;
}
```
Reason:
The fix checks if either `NETIF_F_IP_CSUM` or `NETIF_F_IPV6_CSUM` is set along with `NETIF_F_HW_CSUM`. If neither is set, it disables `NETIF_F_HW_TLS_TX`. This allows devices that support IP and IPv6 checksums to retain TLS TX offload functionality, addressing the issue caused by the previous restriction.

